{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-23T10:04:05.325Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6fe7ba654eae068ba842efbc","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.330","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-5mstyv"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"CodeFactor reports zizmor dangerous-triggers on release-reliability.yml's workflow_run trigger as a new critical issue on every PR that touches a workflow"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"CodeFactor's check on PR #1772 (and on Dependabot PR #1771) failed with one critical issue: zizmor rule dangerous-triggers at .github/workflows/release-reliability.yml line 4, 'workflow_run is almost always used insecurely'. Neither PR changed that file; CodeFactor re-runs zizmor over the workflow set whenever a PR touches any workflow, so every Actions pin update hits it. The trigger is deliberate and already hardened: the job runs only for runs on the default branch (head_branch guard), checks out the default branch rather than the triggering run's code, keeps persist-credentials false, grants only contents/actions/issues read, and downloads no artifact from the triggering run. Fix: record that justification beside the trigger with zizmor's inline suppression so the finding is closed at its source with the reason, instead of being re-reported on unrelated PRs. Duplicate check: searched CodeFactor workflow security finding hosted analysis workflow trigger; pm-92if owns CodeFactor code findings, nothing owns this workflow rule."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Chore"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:ci","codefactor","security","supply-chain"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-23T10:04:05.325Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-23T10:04:05.325Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":15},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"release-reliability.yml carries a zizmor dangerous-triggers suppression on the workflow_run trigger with the hardening rationale beside it; CodeFactor reports no new issue for PR #1772's final head"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-92if"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"low"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"A PR that touches a workflow no longer fails CodeFactor on the deliberate, hardened workflow_run trigger"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"bb4060973f1418a57f2a19de97229ae6f312e078d0e17ab0f41e820cf3eca6e9","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"2358e00125d97edd2ea3107755db2b52fb6e66bead044a02df39630e1fa11545"}
